rarer: one of the two colours clearly ahead of the other (by .15 or more); deep debt, where the money is spoken for; great wealth, where the sum makes no difference
times: Perhaps 1 life in 6 meets it, at any age (estimate)
gap: 5-15
scene: Money {N} did not expect lands all at once: a refund, a gift, a small win. {friend} is already planning a weekend away, and the savings jar sits on the shelf.
scene B: {N} can see exactly where it should go: toward the thing {N} is building. And {friend}'s weekend sounds wonderful.
scene R: {N} can already taste the weekend. A sensible voice at the back of {Ns} head keeps saying the word later.
scene W: {N} thinks first of what is owed and who needs it. Then {friend} rings again, laughing, and {N} wants to laugh too.
scene U: {N} opens a spreadsheet in {Ns} head: saved, it grows; spent, it is a memory. Both columns look good.
scene G: Good luck comes and goes like rain. {N} wonders whether to store it up or let it soak in where it falls.
- B | put every bit of it toward the thing you are building | v: achievement, security | chance: 60
- R | spend it on the weekend away, and enjoy every minute | v: hedonism, stimulation | chance: 60
- W | pay back what you owe first, then think about the rest | v: conformity, security | mark: kept your word | chance: 70
- U | make a plan for every part of it before spending anything | v: self-direction, security | chance: 70
- G | give a share to the household, and let the rest wait | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 70
- R>B | go on the weekend, and use it to meet people who could help your plans | v: hedonism, achievement | chance: 55
- W>G | put it into the family's shared pot for the next lean month | v: security, benevolence | chance: 64
- U>W | find out who on the street needs it more, and quietly help | v: universalism, benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 64
- B>U | spend it on a course or a tool that will earn its cost back twice | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 64
- G>R | wake up on the day, and do whatever your gut says | v: hedonism, self-direction | chance: 64
works: The money goes somewhere {N} is glad of a year later.
works: {N} gets both a good memory and a little left over.
fails: The money is gone within the month, and {N} cannot quite say where.
fails: {N} holds on so tightly that the chance for something good slips past.

== the yearly trip with the whole group
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 14-110
tone: mixed
life: friends, travel
horizon: months
roles: friend
earth: your group goes to the same place every summer and has booked your place, but this year you want to go your own way
requires: R and G both above .22, one of them up .04 or more over the last two years; at most once every five years for this pair
likelier: juvenile and young adult years; a close group of long-standing friends or a close family; a recent taste of travelling alone; much Red and Green in the color history
rarer: one of the two colours clearly ahead of the other (by .15 or more); no close group; little money or time for travel
times: Perhaps 1 life in 8 meets it, most often between 15 and 40 (estimate)
gap: 5-15
scene: The whole group goes to the same lake every summer, and {friend} has booked {Ns} place already. This year {N} wants to go somewhere alone, and nobody in the group has ever said no.
scene R: {N} wants the open road and nobody's plans but {Ns} own. And {N} can already picture the empty place by the fire at the lake.
scene G: The lake is where this group has always belonged together. {N} loves it, and something in {N} wants new ground too.
scene W: {N} said yes to the lake last year, without thinking. Now {N} wonders whether that was a promise, and whether it can bend.
scene U: {N} works out what a solo trip could teach them, and what a year away from the lake might cost the friendships.
scene B: {N} wants this summer for {Ns} own ends. The group will take it personally, and {N} weighs whether that matters.
- R | tell the group you are going your own way this year, and go | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 60
- G | go with the group to the lake, as you always do | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 60
- W | keep your word to the group this year, and tell them early about next year | v: conformity | chance: 70
- U | work out whether you could do both, and draw up the dates | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- B | go on your own, and get your deposit back from the group first | v: self-direction, power | chance: 70
- R>G | talk the whole group into somewhere new this year, and go together | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 55
- W>U | ask the group to agree a fair way to choose the place each year | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 64
- U>B | plan a solo trip so cheap and clever that you lose nothing by it | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 64
- B>R | book your own trip for the same week, and tell them at the last minute | v: self-direction | mark: broke your word | chance: 64
- G>W | go with the group, and take on looking after the camp for everyone | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 64
works: {N} has the summer they needed, and the group is still there when they come back.
works: The friendships come out of it looser in a good way, with room for everyone.
fails: The group goes on without {N}, and the jokes from the lake are ones {N} was not there for.
fails: {N} goes along and spends the week wishing they were somewhere else.

== a front garden left to grow
tier: inner
stages: all
age: 14-110
tone: mixed
life: home, neighbours
horizon: months
roles: a neighbour
earth: the street's rules say front gardens are kept trim, and yours has gone half wild with bees and birds
requires: G and W both above .22, one of them up .04 or more over the last two years; at most once every five years for this pair
likelier: a home with a garden or shared green space; a street or block with a residents' committee; mature and elder years; much Green and White in the color history
rarer: one of the two colours clearly ahead of the other (by .15 or more); a flat with no outdoor space; a street with no rules or committee
times: Perhaps 1 life in 10 meets it, most often from the thirties on (estimate)
gap: 5-15
scene: The residents' rules say front gardens are kept trim. {Ns} has gone half wild, full of bees and birds, and a neighbour has just slipped the rules through the door with a polite note.
scene G: {N} loves the hum of it on a warm morning. And {N} knows the street is a kind of garden too, one that grows on its rules.
scene W: Rules are what let a street live together, and {N} has always kept them. Yet the wild patch feels like something owed to the bees.
scene U: {N} reads the note twice and starts weighing it: what the rule is for, and what the wild garden does better.
scene B: It is {Ns} garden, bought and paid for. Still, {N} has to live beside these people for years, and they know it.
scene R: The note makes {Ns} cheeks burn. {N} wants to march next door, and also wants, somewhere underneath, to keep the peace.
- G | leave it wild, because the bees were here before the rules | v: universalism | chance: 60
- W | cut it back to the rule, neatly, this weekend | v: conformity | chance: 60
- U | read up on the bees and birds, and write the committee a careful letter | v: universalism, self-direction | chance: 70
- B | ignore the note, because your garden is nobody else's business | v: self-direction, power | chance: 70
- R | knock on the neighbour's door today and have it out face to face | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 70
- G>W | trim a neat strip along the path, and let the rest grow as it wants | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 55
- W>U | ask the committee to change the rule so wild gardens are allowed | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 64
- U>B | find the gap in the wording that lets the garden stay as it is | v: self-direction, power | chance: 64
- B>R | offer the neighbour a favour in trade, and keep the garden free | v: power, self-direction | chance: 64
- R>G | throw a garden party for the street, and let them see the bees for themselves | v: stimulation, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 64
works: The garden stays, in some shape, and the street is on better terms than before.
works: {N} and the neighbour find a middle that both can live with.
fails: The note becomes a letter from the committee, and then a second one.
fails: {N} gives way, and the bees are gone by midsummer.
